01:06:10.260 --> 01:06:11.860
You mean .38s were called for before?

01:06:12.180 --> 01:06:13.720
Yeah, they made a row about it.

01:06:13.760 --> 01:06:14.320
Who insisted?

01:06:14.400 --> 01:06:15.540
Okay, coming up.

01:06:15.800 --> 01:06:16.680
Come on with me.

01:06:19.680 --> 01:06:20.600
Listen, I've got it.

01:06:21.380 --> 01:06:22.560
This is Bill, the property man.

01:06:22.930 --> 01:06:24.490
He tells me on the day that Brent was murdered,

01:06:24.610 --> 01:06:27.430
he was definitely ordered to give all the extras .38 caliber guns.

01:06:27.610 --> 01:06:27.770
Yeah?

01:06:27.970 --> 01:06:28.390
Did you get it?

01:06:28.570 --> 01:06:29.910
.38 caliber guns were ordered.

01:06:30.000 --> 01:06:33.040
Now, if Bill had supplied them, we'd have never known that it wasn't an accident.

01:06:39.150 --> 01:06:39.870
But he didn't.

01:06:40.380 --> 01:06:41.800
He substituted .45s.

01:06:41.940 --> 01:06:43.120
That's how we knew it was a murder.

01:06:43.710 --> 01:06:45.550
Now, the fellow who ordered those .38s...

01:06:45.860 --> 01:06:46.940
Say, who ordered those guns?

01:06:47.200 --> 01:06:47.920
Go ahead, Bill.

01:06:48.020 --> 01:06:48.340
Tell him.

01:06:48.570 --> 01:06:50.430
Well, it was Mr....

01:06:50.430 --> 01:06:51.210
Everybody stand up!

01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:00.240
All right.

01:08:31.980 --> 01:08:32.980
Avery.

01:08:33.292 --> 01:08:34.192
Mr. Avery.

01:08:34.252 --> 01:08:35.532
So he's the one that ordered the guns?

01:08:35.712 --> 01:08:37.792
Yes, and like a fool, I told you about him under the microphone.

01:08:38.032 --> 01:08:39.312
He was listening in with the earphones.

01:08:39.628 --> 01:08:40.468
So it was him.

01:08:43.308 --> 01:08:44.828
Don't look at him now. He's dead.

01:08:45.996 --> 01:08:46.996
I'm dead.

01:08:47.308 --> 01:08:47.808
Yes!

01:08:48.876 --> 01:08:49.716
Oh God!

01:08:52.332 --> 01:08:54.332
A woman at the Cliffside Inn, huh?

01:08:59.660 --> 01:08:59.980
Hey, Harry.

01:09:00.000 --> 01:09:01.300
Come on, come with me.

01:09:01.740 --> 01:09:06.240
Got him.

01:09:11.590 --> 01:09:12.510
There's your man.

01:09:13.050 --> 01:09:13.670
Who is he?

01:09:20.200 --> 01:09:22.910
For this, you despicable cad.

01:09:23.350 --> 01:09:24.870
So, you're a policeman, huh?

01:09:37.960 --> 01:09:42.420
I think I owe apologies, Miss Lane, and to you, too.

01:09:42.770 --> 01:09:44.890
I'm sorry I was unpleasant.

01:09:45.430 --> 01:09:47.210
You know, at first I could have sworn it was you.

01:09:47.410 --> 01:09:49.130
I knew it, and it made me quite angry.

01:09:50.100 --> 01:09:52.260
But you're much more clever than I gave you credit for.

01:09:52.440 --> 01:09:54.380
Well, that sounds like a new contract.

01:09:56.090 --> 01:09:57.570
We'll talk about that later.

01:10:01.276 --> 01:10:01.836
Oh, wow.

01:10:02.620 --> 01:10:03.060
Lieutenant.

01:10:03.964 --> 01:10:07.184
Would you mind telling me why it is the detectives always wear their hats?

01:10:07.356 --> 01:10:08.536
Even in the presence of ladies?

01:10:09.052 --> 01:10:09.772
Well, sure.

01:10:10.524 --> 01:10:14.484
That's so we won't have anything in our hands or arms in case we have to use them.

01:10:15.516 --> 01:10:16.616
That's one for the book.

01:10:17.020 --> 01:10:18.580
Do you mind if I write it in right now?
